WEB WILL DO / WON’T DO — REQUIRED ON EVERY PRODUCT WEB
PAGE

\================================================================================



Principle

\- Every Nivo78 product web presence states plainly
what the product will do for the user and what it will not do — before download
or store install.

\- The goal is trust: a customer who reads the page
should not hit a negative surprise about scope,

  automation,
sync, tiers, or handoffs after they install.

\- Same promise on in-repo hub, hosted product page,
and support scope summary; legal pages link here instead of duplicating full
lists.



Required pages and sections



Product hub — code/Website/{product}/index.html (and
hosted https\://nivo78.com/{product}/)

\- philosophy-tagline when accurate (local-first, account,
sync, analytics — adapt with plain exceptions).

\- h2: “What {Product} will do for you” — bullet list
from MARKETING\_COPY.txt (minimum 4 bullets covering core job,
validation/handoff, offline/local, collect-once or equivalent when applicable).

\- h2: “What {Product} won’t do for you” — bullet list
from MARKETING\_COPY.txt (minimum 4 bullets including handoff honesty — e.g. no
store upload when preparation-only; plus family boundaries that apply).

\- Recommended: “Good fit if you” and/or “Skip if”
short blocks for audience clarity.

\- Legal & support links panel unchanged (Privacy,
Terms, Support center).



Support center — support/index.html

\- philosophy-banner (local-first / data-on-device) —
already required.

\- h2: “What {Product} will and won’t do” — condensed
won’t-do boundaries (minimum 3 bullets) plus one-line will-do summary OR
explicit link to product page full lists.

\- Must not contradict product page will/won’t lists.



Privacy and terms

\- No full marketing will/won’t sections required —
link to support or product page for product scope when mentioning capabilities.



In-app alignment

\- About, first-run scope, or upgrade copy should
reflect the same will/won’t boundaries as web — TRUTH text test traces claims
across surfaces.



Verify and audit

\- Website verify script checks index.html for will-do
and won’t-do section headings (or equivalent labeled headings).

\- Nivo78 app.txt SCOPE-WEB vector audits product hub
and support scope sections.

\- COVERAGE vector checks bidirectional completeness —
every shipped capability in will-do; every won’t-do boundary enforced in code.





