WEB COPY, HONESTY, AND APP ALIGNMENT

\================================================================================



Copy–code parity (mandatory)

\- Privacy policy describes what the engine actually
stores: plain vs encrypted vs blocked vs never stored.

\- Terms effective date and version match in-app
ApaLegalCopy (or product equivalent) and acceptance gate.

\- Platform scope on web matches shipped binaries
(desktop vs mobile companion vs unsupported form factors).

\- “What the product does / does not do” on web matches
in-app Help and export/handoff behavior — no implied upload, sync, or
automation.

\- No “coming soon,” “planned,” or roadmap language on
legal/support pages unless capability is shipped in this build.



Will do / won’t do on product web pages (mandatory —
see MARKETING AND SCOPE COPY section)

\- Every product ships scannable “will do for you” and
“won’t do for you” sections on the product hub and hosted product page — not
optional marketing fluff.

\- Support page includes at least a won’t-do boundary
summary or link to the full scope on the product page.

\- Privacy and terms pages do not need full marketing
lists — they cross-link to support or product page for scope.



Security and privacy content layering

\- Support page: plain-language “what is encrypted vs
plain” and “blocked from plain saves.”

\- Privacy page: full policy including optional technical
specifications section (crypto detail belongs here, not primary Help hub rows).

\- In-app Data security / Help summaries must not
contradict privacy HTML — run updocs after engine security copy changes.



Last updated / effective dates

\- Engine legal copy object is the source of truth
(APA: ApaLegalCopy.kt — PRIVACY\_LAST\_UPDATED, EFFECTIVE\_DATE, TERMS\_VERSION;
product title from ApaProductIdentity.PRODUCT\_TITLE).

\- Privacy: “Last updated” at top MUST equal
ApaLegalCopy.PRIVACY\_LAST\_UPDATED (or product equivalent); bump both when
privacy policy changes.

\- Terms: “Effective date” and “Version” at top MUST
equal ApaLegalCopy.EFFECTIVE\_DATE and ApaLegalCopy.TERMS\_VERSION; bump
TERMS\_VERSION when terms change materially and re-run legal gate.

\- Privacy policy-product-name text MUST equal the
public product title constant in engine code.

\- Release verify (verify-apa-website.ps1 WEB LEGAL
SYNC + ApaInRepoLegalSecurityCopyTest) fails when HTML dates, version, or
product name drift from engine constants.

\- Privacy changes section explains re-consent when
terms reference updated policy.





